    "md5": "9fbd983c3ce80c0673ccfc4088cf3819",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1839,
    "chunk_text": "One of them is the Provincial Councils Elections (Amendment) Bill that I presented. Like I mentioned, adopt that as a Government Bill. I have no issue. You take up my Private Members' Bill to amend the Provincial Councils Act as a Government Bill, pass that and fix a date for the Provincial Councils Elections. We do not have to fix a specific date; let us, at least, say within this period of the year. But, that assurance has to be given and that promise must be kept because in this country, the problem is that so many promises had been given to the Tamil people, but none had been kept.\n\nTherefore, Hon. President, please look into the matter of the human skeletons unearthed with utmost importance. Try and involve international investigators and observers in that so that our people would have some sort of faith in the process. Allocate enough money. Those crimes were not committed by you; those crimes were not committed when you all were in power; it is not your party that was in power when those were committed. Why are you trying to protect them? If somebody had committed those atrocities in the 90s, let us all work together to find who the culprits are. We have always voiced our concerns about the Matale mass graves; we have stood by you all; we have always raised our concerns about Colonel Gotabaya Rajapaksa\u2019s involvement in the Matale mass graves. So, we have stood by you; we have stood by your revolution and your cadres. Why are you now hesitant to, at least, try to deliver justice to our people? Among those skeletons that were found, the experts on the site had said, some could have belonged to a child who was three months old! So, Sir, why is the Government hesitant to investigate into this?\n\nThen, the issue of missing persons is also very similar to this. We have raised these issues on every possible"
