    "chunk_text": "At the outset, let me take a few moments to congratulate the newly elected councillors of the Colombo Municipal Council. We hope that they would live up to the expectations of the citizens of this beautiful City of Colombo, of which I, too, am a citizen. So, my best wishes go out to all of them, to all the elected office bearers of the Council - the Mayor and the Deputy Mayor - and the elected members, in delivering what the citizens of the City of Colombo expect.\n\nSir, there is another equally alarming trend that deserves our immediate consideration. That is the growing and largely unregulated culture of gym-based fitness among our youth, both young men and women. Across our cities, suburbs and even the villages, we are witnessing the rapid mushrooming of gyms. While promoting fitness and heathy living is commendable, the reality on the ground is far more complex and worrying. Many of these establishments have sprung up without any oversight, certification and qualified instructors. Sir, I must stress the point that we are allowing our youth to walk into these unregulated gyms and consume so-called muscle-building formulas, supplements and sometimes, outright anabolic steroids without any medical guidance or knowledge of their long-term consequences. These substances, often imported, unregulated and purchased online, are widely marketed as harmless protein powders or fitness boosters. But, the truth is far more sinister. Sir, you know too well that studies have shown that the misuse of such supplements could lead to irreversible hormonal imbalances, liver damage, renal damage,"
