    "chunk_text": "Sir, there is another equally alarming trend that deserves our immediate consideration. That is the growing and largely unregulated culture of gym-based fitness among our youth, both young men and women. Across our cities, suburbs and even the villages, we are witnessing the rapid mushrooming of gyms. While promoting fitness and heathy living is commendable, the reality on the ground is far more complex and worrying. Many of these establishments have sprung up without any oversight, certification and qualified instructors. Sir, I must stress the point that we are allowing our youth to walk into these unregulated gyms and consume so-called muscle-building formulas, supplements and sometimes, outright anabolic steroids without any medical guidance or knowledge of their long-term consequences. These substances, often imported, unregulated and purchased online, are widely marketed as harmless protein powders or fitness boosters. But, the truth is far more sinister. Sir, you know too well that studies have shown that the misuse of such supplements could lead to irreversible hormonal imbalances, liver damage, renal damage,\n\nSir, we must not wait for this issue to spiral into a national health crisis. If we fail, we would be condemning an entire generation for a future of chronic illnesses, psychological trauma and broken dreams. This is not merely a sports issue, but a matter of our national health, of youth development and therefore, warrants our collective moral responsibility."
