    "md5": "ae126ff1de9ce1ef7f4478d635271f99",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1926,
    "chunk_text": "1. What measures have been taken to ensure transparency and stakeholder engagement, especially with trade unions, exporters and civil society during the two rounds of GSP Plus negotiations? What specific labour law reforms has the Government agreed to or what specific labour law reforms has the Government been asked to undertake?\n\n3. What assessments have been conducted to determine how potential changes to GSP Plus would impact on small and medium-sized exporters, especially in the apparel, fisheries and agri-based sectors?\n\n4. The recently enacted Online Safety Act has sparked concern with regard to its potential effect on freedom of expression, media independence and digital rights. Will the Government consider reviewing or amending the Act to include safeguards? Has stakeholder consultation taken place on this matter?\n\n5. In the event that the GSP Plus benefits are suspended or negotiations collapse, what is the Government\u2019s contingency plan to protect export industries and employment?\n\nThen, the third part of the Question is related to free trade with the United Kingdom because of the fact that the United Kingdom has entered into a Free Trade Agreement with India. So, I am trying to protect Sri Lanka\u2019s interests. Therefore, I would like to ask the following questions:\n\n1. Has the Government initiated or considered launching negotiations for a bilateral trade or market access agreement with the United Kingdom to ensure competitiveness for Sri Lankan exporters?\n\n2. Why did Sri Lanka not proactively engage in trade discussions with the UK, especially when the India-UK FTA negotiations were publicly known and ongoing for nearly a decade?\n\n2497 2498\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0dc1\u0db8\u0dca\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\n\n3. Given our longstanding ties with the United Kingdom and our shared membership in the Commonwealth, why has Sri Lanka not sought \"priority country\" status to expedite a Trade Agreement with the UK?"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
