    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "509453bf6821fae6c638f25d13ec3587",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2082,
    "chunk_text": "3. Given our longstanding ties with the United Kingdom and our shared membership in the Commonwealth, why has Sri Lanka not sought \"priority country\" status to expedite a Trade Agreement with the UK?\n\n5. Does Sri Lanka have a data-driven strategy to assess and respond to the potential market erosion caused by the India-UK FTA? How will intelligence be used to protect and promote our exports to the UK market?\n\nThank you.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dc3\u0dab\u0da0\u0dcf\u0dcf \u0dba \u0dc4\u0dcf \u0dc2\u0dca\u0da8\u0da7 \u0dc3\u0dd6\u0dbb\u0dd2\u0dba\u0dda\u0dc0\u0db4\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0db8 \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dca\u0dcf \u0dc3\u0db8\u0dd4\u0daf\u0dbd\u0dca \u0dc4 \u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0db8 \u0db8\u0dca\u0db4\u0dcf\u0daf\u0db1 \u0db1\u0dd2\u0dc0\u0dba \u0da2\u200d \u0d85\u0db8\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0db8\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 (\u0b95\u0bb2\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bbf) \u0bb9\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0bb7\u0ba3 \u0b9a\u0bc2\u0bbe\u0bbf\u0baf\u0baa\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0baa\u0bb0\u0bc1\u0bae - \u0ba8\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bbf, \u0ba4\u0bbf\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b9f\u0bb2\u0bcd \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf \u0b85\u0b95\u0bae\u0b9a\u0bcd\u0b9a\u0bb0\u0bcd) (The Hon. (Dr.) Harshana Suriyapperuma - Deputy Minister of Finance and Planning) Hon. Deputy Chairperson of Committees, the Hon. Member has asked not just a Question, but a list of questions; there are 16 of them. They were received a little late. - [Interruption] Yes, sure. But, an Answer has been prepared. There are three major sections to this Question. The first part relates to US tariffs, the second part, to the GSP and the third part, to the ongoing trade discussions with the UK.\n\nHon. Member, with regard to the US tariff discussions, many areas have already been discussed. The Answer to the first part of the Question is as follows:\n\n1. Discussions are ongoing and are yet to be finalized.\n\n2. The same position applies to taking concrete steps. There are alternatives that have been identified, but a finality is yet to be reached because discussions are ongoing.\n\n3. With regard to an updated export strategy, we are looking at new markets and new products, obviously focusing on expansion through diversification et cetera. So, multiple factors have been considered, but a finality, as I mentioned earlier, is yet to be reached. It is a mutual benefit arrangement. Discussions are ongoing with very positive engagement from both sides."
  },
