    "md5": "1eee7cfca42ea23e1518e25a6f9e8759",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1832,
    "chunk_text": "3. With regard to an updated export strategy, we are looking at new markets and new products, obviously focusing on expansion through diversification et cetera. So, multiple factors have been considered, but a finality, as I mentioned earlier, is yet to be reached. It is a mutual benefit arrangement. Discussions are ongoing with very positive engagement from both sides.\n\ndevelopments to date, we have a very good relationship and very good ongoing discussions.\n\n5. In terms of trade disruptions, obviously, trade disruptions sometimes bring about opportunities as well. During these negotiations and discussions, we have identified opportunities that Sri Lanka could explore further.\n\nSo, it is a good outcome that we have in some of the areas. Obviously, there are also challenges, given the current economic calamity and the situation that the country is going through. But, we are expecting a good outcome, as I mentioned earlier.\n\n6. Actually, we explored other regional alliances. It is a continuous engagement. We will continuously be exploring the facilities and opportunities that are out there.\n\nThe second part of the Question mainly relates to European Union's GSP Plus negotiations. The Answer to those five questions is in a concise or summarized form. It is an ongoing process. The partners of the European Union had been here and we had engaged in preliminary discussions with them. There has been progress on those fronts. Our view is to engage multiple stakeholders, get their views and ideas also when responding to these engagements and the issues that have been identified, focusing on improvements. Particularly, with regard to the issues that you have mentioned relating to the Online Safety Act and various other provisions you have identified, we are exploring alternative approaches to provide solutions."
  },
