    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "aef6c1d800b640d061fb8dd0701b0762",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2002,
    "chunk_text": "The second part of the Question mainly relates to European Union's GSP Plus negotiations. The Answer to those five questions is in a concise or summarized form. It is an ongoing process. The partners of the European Union had been here and we had engaged in preliminary discussions with them. There has been progress on those fronts. Our view is to engage multiple stakeholders, get their views and ideas also when responding to these engagements and the issues that have been identified, focusing on improvements. Particularly, with regard to the issues that you have mentioned relating to the Online Safety Act and various other provisions you have identified, we are exploring alternative approaches to provide solutions.\n\nThen the third part of the Question relates to free trade agreements with the United Kingdom. Once again, the discussions are ongoing; in relation to that, several discussions have already taken place. Hon. Deputy Chairperson of Committees, the Answers are as follows:\n\n1. The Government of Sri Lanka has consistently expressed its interest in establishing trade agreements or market access arrangements with the UK, recognizing the importance of maintaining and enhancing the competitiveness of Sri Lankan exporters in the UK market, particularly following the UK\u2019s departure from the European Union.\n\nSri Lanka has conveyed its interest through multiple channels, including official channels. At every opportunity, the Government has emphasized the potential mutual benefits of such arrangements, especially for key export sectors such as apparel, tea, and rubber-based products.\n\n2. As stated in Answer to 1 above, Sri Lanka has, in fact, been proactive in engaging with the United Kingdom to express its interest in market access engagements, discussions and arrangements.\n\n2499 2500\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dba\u0dc0\u0dd3 \u0d9a\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0da7\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf]\n\n2025 \u0da2\u0dd4\u0db1\u0dd2 17\n\nThose efforts have included consistent outreach through various engagements through official means."
  },
