    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "95d06cadd9185f5501d5c0d1c89dac75",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1969,
    "chunk_text": "2. As stated in Answer to 1 above, Sri Lanka has, in fact, been proactive in engaging with the United Kingdom to express its interest in market access engagements, discussions and arrangements.\n\n2499 2500\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dba\u0dc0\u0dd3 \u0d9a\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0da7\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf]\n\n2025 \u0da2\u0dd4\u0db1\u0dd2 17\n\nThose efforts have included consistent outreach through various engagements through official means.\n\n4. Government continues to explore and identify all possible mechanisms and avenues to engage in dialogues continuously.\n\n5. The Government of Sri Lanka is closely monitoring the India-United Kingdom Free Trade Agreement and its contents.\n\nWe observe that the detailed provisions of the Agreement such as tariff reduction schedules, rules of origin, quota allocations and service commitments have not yet been made public to the extent for us to make certain decisions and to make further engagements. Therefore, we will arrange a comprehensive Impact Analysis, focusing on its impact on our major sectors. If there is any overlapping export interests into the market, we will look into those and continue to explore synergies. Hon. Member, I am sure there will be additional opportunities coming up as well, given that Sri Lanka is located next to India. Therefore, we will continue to explore those opportunities and synergies for us to co-operate and collaborate for mutual benefit. We do not anticipate any immediate challenges or threats emerging from that Agreement. However, as I mentioned, we will continue to monitor, analyse the details and prepare a detailed response from the Government side in order to facilitate our exporters and industries to continue to have access to those markets, thereby enabling our industries to grow.\n\nHon. Deputy Chairperson of Committees, this is particularly important for the production economy that we have mentioned. The Government will continue to focus on supporting and facilitating those industries in these areas.\n\nThank you"
  },
