    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "62e1add026eea9171cbcd13f0f283237",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2268,
    "chunk_text": "\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dc4\u0dcf \u0dc2\u0dca\u0da8\u0da7 \u0dc3\u0dd6\u0dbb\u0dd2\u0dba\u0dda\u0dc0\u0db4\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0db8 \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dca\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0bb9\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0bb7\u0ba3 \u0b9a\u0bc2\u0bbe\u0bbf\u0baf\u0baa\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0baa\u0bb0\u0bc1\u0bae) (The Hon. Harshana Suriyapperuma) Thank you very much for highlighting that fact in your clarification. Yes, evolving global dynamics focus on and push countries like Sri Lanka to look for new solutions and innovative approaches to some of the challenges. The challenges are not only trade-related, but also due to other ongoing tensions in various regions. Some of our traditional markets may be restricted, we may have restricted access and cost escalations in\n\n2501 2502\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0dc1\u0db8\u0dca\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\n\nThank you.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dc3\u0dab\u0da0\u0dcf\u0dcf \u0dba \u0dc4\u0dcf \u0dc2\u0dca\u0da8\u0da7 \u0dc3\u0dd6\u0dbb\u0dd2\u0dba\u0dda\u0dc0\u0db4\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0db8 \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dca\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 (\u0b95\u0bb2\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbf\u0ba4\u0bbf) \u0bb9\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0bb7\u0ba3 \u0b9a\u0bc2\u0bbe\u0bbf\u0baf\u0baa\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0baa\u0bb0\u0bc1\u0bae) (The Hon. (Dr.) Harshana Suriyapperuma) Hon. Deputy Chairperson of Committees, I will take this on as the last question seeking clarification. As I said before, we know that our competitiveness was hampered over a long period of time, not because of lack of creativity among our entrepreneurs and businesses, but because they were not competitive enough to go into international markets with our energy costs being so high and our infrastructure supporting in terms of finance cost was so high. Therefore, they could not compete with some of the countries in other regions, which were much more competitive. That is why the present Government, in its Manifesto, very clearly mentioned that over a period of time, we would reduce the energy prices by nearly 30 per cent, allowing our exporters to compete freely and effectively in the global as well as the regional markets. So, our approach is to reduce energy prices.\n\nThen, our digitization process - once again you mentioned the SVAT, Hon. Member - is to ensure that we have a seamless process. That is why several activities are lined up back-to-back to support those sectors. The Government has taken decisions and laid out a plan in place to ensure that those sectors are supported as and when necessary amidst these global challenges.\n\nMadam, I will limit answering questions up to that point. Thank You."
  },
