    "chunk_size_bytes": 2093,
    "chunk_text": "In terms of Article 41B of the Constitution of Sri Lanka, amended by the Twenty First and Twenty Second Amendments to the Constitution, the Constitutional Council is entrusted with the task of recommending of members to several independent Commissions. These Commissions play a vital role in safeguarding the integrity, transparency and accountability of public administration.\n\nBased on publicly available information, the following 10 Commissions are currently considered independent or semi-independent.\n\n1. Election Commission\n\n2. Public Service Commission\n\n2849 2850\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 (\u0dca\u0da0\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dba) \u0dc4\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dc2\u0dca\u0da8\u0da7 \u0dd6 \u0dbb\u0dd2\u0dba\u0dda\u0dc1\u0db4\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0db8 \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf]\n\n2025 \u0da2\u0dd4\u0db1\u0dd2 20\n\n4. Audit Service Commission\n\n5. Human Rights Commission of Sri Lanka\n\n6. Commission to Investigate Allegations of\n\nBribery or Corruption - CIABOC\n\n7. Finance Commission\n\n8. Delimitation Commission\n\n9. National Procurement Commission\n\n10. Public Utilities Commission of Sri Lanka -\n\nPUCSL- which is semi-independent.\n\nWhile these Commissions derive their authority from the Constitution or enabling statutes, it appears that many of them function without publicly available or standardized Standard Operating Procedures - SOPs - governing internal operations such as recruitment, disciplinary processes, complaint management and public engagement. This has led to inconsistencies and an ad hoc policy framework in their administration.\n\nIn view of the above, I seek clarification from the Hon. Prime Minister as Minister in charge of Constitutional Affairs by raising the following questions:\n\n1. Is the list of Commissions stated above accurate? If not, how many independent Commissions have been established under the Constitution of Sri Lanka, including those under Article 41B?\n\n2. Have all these independent Commissions adopted Standard Operating Procedures - SOPs - or internal administrative guidelines to govern? Has it got approval from Parliament or is it only an internal policy?\n\n3. If such Standard Operating Procedures have been adopted,\n\n\uf0b7 which Commissions have made them publicly"
  },
  {
