    "chunk_text": "Among the main promises given to the people in the Election Manifesto \u201cA Thriving Nation, a Beautiful Life\u201d of the National People\u2019s Power was the commitment to ensure justice for human rights violations, including immediately revealing the truth about the Easter attack.\n\nThe National People's Power must clarify to this august Assembly why it has failed to fulfil the pledges and promises given to the international community, His Eminence Cardinal Malcolm Ranjith and the victims of the Easter attack. Therefore, I expect answers from the Government to the following questions that have arisen and remain unanswered regarding the Easter attack:\n\n1. According to a statement made by His Excellency the President\n\nAnura Kumara Dissanayake, which appeared in an article published in 'Economy Next' magazine on February 12, 2021, the Presidential Commission Report on the Easter Attacks should be immediately presented to Parliament. \"\n\nThat was stated in his statement, as reported in the \"Economy Next\" article of 12th of February, 2021.\n\n\"Although four years have passed since this proposal of His Excellency the President, why has this report not been presented to this House yet?\n\n2. Did the Attorney-General's Department intervene to grant bail\n\nto Sivanesathurai Chandrakanthan alias Pillayan, who was identified by the Minister of Public Security as the mastermind of the Easter Sunday attack in this august Assembly? Was this prevented due to the objections of the Criminal Investigation Department?\n\n3. How many DNA reports of Sara Jasmine were submitted? Will\n\nyou specify the dates on which these reports were submitted, separately? Do institutions in our country possess the necessary facilities to conduct such DNA testing again?\n\n251 252\n\n\u0dad\u0ddc\u0dca\u0dd2\u0dc4\u0db8\u0dca\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\n\n4. Is there a confirmed report regarding the disappearance of a"
