    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/documents/hansard/1752660241032216.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2025-07-09-2025-07-09-0203",
    "chunk_index": 203,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "7db0f75bf6251b93da2f320d7d046a8c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1741,
    "chunk_text": "\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0da2\u0dd3.\u0da2\u0dd3. \u0dc0\u0db4\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dca\u0db1\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0dbd\u0db8\u0dca \u0db8\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dad\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bc8\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bc8\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9c\u0bc0.\u0b9c\u0bc0. \u0ba4\u0baa\u0bc6\u0bbe\u0ba9\u0bcd\u0ba9\u0bae\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bb2\u0bae\u0bcd) (The Hon. G.G. Ponnambalam) Hon. Presiding Member, there is a very important maxim in the legal jurisprudence which says that justice must not only be done, but it must be seen to be done. That maxim, I wish to start my speech with because when\n\n331 332\n\n\u0dad\u0ddc\u0dca\u0dd2\u0dc4\u0db8\u0dca\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\n\nSir, this, I am saying because I agree that on a crime where the State structure is an accused party, where the State is seen as an accomplice or its complicity is the biggest accusation that is being made, the State cannot investigate itself through an internal investigation. It goes against the very nature, the very core principle of natural justice. How can an accused party investigate itself?\n\nThat is why, Sir, whilst the fifth point of the Motion talks of an independent Prosecutor\u2019s Office that has\n\ninternational assistance, I have disagreed with that. My view is that on a crime such as the Easter Sunday attack, where the State is an accused party, the investigation must be international in character. You do not have power over that State structure. The Minister of Justice and National Integration, because his name was registered in Parliament as \"Dr.\", that he had got a PhD, had to go to the CID to make a complaint because he suspected that there was sabotage. That is how deep the political influence has been. We all know that. So, under those circumstances, Sir, mark my words, if you all want genuine justice, you would never get it. You would never get it because you do not have the control of the State in an independent manner. That is the truth."
  },
