    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/documents/hansard/1754386160089643.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2025-07-23-2025-07-23-0170",
    "chunk_index": 170,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "524995a18a53ce73977e2227e0be30c3",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 902,
    "chunk_text": "Madam, this Government that has now come into power makes it a matter of point at every possible opportunity to say that they are not racist like the past governments, especially like the Government in 1983, which did that heinous crime. They say that they do not distinguish on the basis of Sinhala, Tamil, Muslim, Christian and Burgher. Those are the famous phrases that they use.\n\nMadam, today, we are debating Amendments to the Companies Act. I was listening to many speakers. Amendments to the Companies Act are being brought in to ensure prevention of money laundering, prevention of black money and with all of those intentions. I think 20 odd Sections of the Act are being amended and those are things that we welcome. But, I noticed everybody else except the Minister repeatedly concentrating on the notion of preventing terrorism financing and how important these Amendments are towards that."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2025-07-23-2025-07-23",
